  "toolchain": "D:/DevTools/Flutter SDK/flutter/bin/flutter.bat",
  "note": "RED here means the contract and its tests were written FIRST, then run against the unmodified code. The failures are the defects this step found, not a missing file. Both production defects were additionally reproduced by a standalone throwaway probe before any fix, and the probe output is quoted below verbatim.",
  "capability_gap_found": {
    "defect": "canonical bucket `webhook_tests` names a capability that did not exist anywhere under lib/features/account.",
    "evidence": "rg -l 'webhook|Webhook|hmac|HMAC|replay|Replay|timestampTolerance' over lib/features/account and test/features/account returned zero matches for webhook/HMAC/signature at the start of this step. The only `webhook` token in lib/ was lib/core/capabilities/reactivation_dependency_map.dart, which is unrelated to provider callbacks.",
    "consequence": "An inbound billing or provider callback had no signature check, no timestamp window, and no replay guard. Anything that reached a callback handler was trusted, and a provider retry of the same delivery could be applied twice.",
    "fix": "lib/features/account/domain/account_center_security_billing_verification.dart adds signatureHeader/verifyWebhook over HMAC-SHA256 of a versioned `v1:<timestamp>:<body>` payload, a constant-time comparison, a declared tolerance window, and an explicit AccountWebhookReplayGuard. It reuses the `crypto` package already in pubspec and the Hmac(sha256, ...) primitive already used by lib/core/security/crypto, so no new dependency was added."
  },
  "probe_before_fix": {
    "file": "test/features/account/domain/zz_probe_11554_test.dart (temporary, deleted after the run; not part of the slice)",
    "command": "flutter test test/features/account/domain/zz_probe_11554_test.dart --no-pub",
    "exit": 0,
    "output_verbatim": [
      "PROBE_A state_at_2020=EntitlementState.granted has=true",
      "PROBE_B reauth=false -> read=rotated audit=[add, replace]"
    ]
  },
  "defect_1_entitlement_issued_before_it_existed": {
    "test": "entitlement_state refuses a time before grantedAt",
    "expected": "EntitlementState.notYetIssued",
    "actual_before_fix": "EntitlementState.granted",
    "root_cause": "AccountCenterSubscriptionEntitlementModel.entitlementStateAt compared ONLY expiresAt. A grant is a signed statement with an issuance time, not a boolean, so evaluating the model at any instant earlier than grantedAt returned granted.",
    "impact": "A caller with a skewed clock, or one replaying a cached evaluation instant, unlocked an entitlement the server had not issued yet. The only production consumer, RightRailAccountSummary.entitlementsAt, tallied it as granted, so the user-visible rail count was also wrong.",
    "fix": "entitlementStateAt now returns the new EntitlementState.notYetIssued when at.isBefore(grant.grantedAt). The rail gained a matching notYetIssued counter rather than folding the new state into expired, because the two mean opposite things to a user."
  },
  "defect_2_api_key_replace_without_reauthentication": {
    "test": "refuses to replace a key while reauthentication is denied",
    "expected": "StateError and the stored secret unchanged",
    "actual_before_fix": "the vault entry was overwritten with 'rotated' and the audit recorded a plain 'replace'",
    "root_cause": "AccountCenterApiKeysManager.replace called vault.save directly. The product spec lists `reveal_or_replace_key` under security_contract.sensitive_actions, and the vault READ path (vault.read, and therefore copyToClipboard) already gated on reauthentication - so a user who could not reveal a key could still silently replace it.",
    "fix": "replace now calls vault.reauthenticate() first; a refusal throws StateError, leaves the stored secret untouched, and is audited as `denied_replace` so the audit trail cannot be read as a successful rotation."
  },
  "matrix_suite_first_run": {
    "command": "flutter test test/features/account/domain/account_center_security_billing_verification_test.dart --no-pub",
    "exit": 1,
    "result": "failed to load",
    "interpretation": "The contract file did not exist, so the suite could not compile. This is the expected RED shape for a new contract and is NOT counted as a defect."
  },
  "live_contracts_suite_first_run": {
    "command": "flutter test test/features/account/domain/account_center_security_billing_live_contracts_test.dart --no-pub",
    "exit": 1,
    "real_defect_failures": [
      "entitlement_state refuses a time before grantedAt - got EntitlementState.granted",
      "refuses to replace a key while reauthentication is denied - no StateError, secret was rotated"
    ],
    "authoring_bugs_of_my_own": [
      "PlanPrice / EntitlementLimit / ManagedSession were written into const lists although their constructors are not const. Fixed in the test, not in production.",
      "One keyFor assertion wrapped a throwing call in expect(...) instead of expect(() => ..., ...), so the ArgumentError escaped the matcher and failed the test. Fixed in the test."
    ]
  },
  "test_authoring_pitfalls_measured": [
    "A test file that fails to COMPILE reports its errors at the top of the output, and `tail` hides them. When a suite shows 'failed to load', read the FIRST error block, not the last lines.",
    "The new enum value EntitlementState.notYetIssued broke the exhaustive switch in the right rail. Dart fails that at compile time, which is the desired outcome, but the rail had to gain a real counter rather than a `case _: break` that would have silently dropped the state."
  ]
}
